## Examples (Ví dụ)

### Ví dụ: Refactoring from Callbacks to Async/Await

**Before:**

```typescript
// Legacy callback-based code
function getUserData(userId, callback) {
  database.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [userId], (err, user) => {
    if (err) return callback(err);
    
    cache.get(`user:${userId}`, (err, cached) => {
      if (err) return callback(err);
      if (cached) return callback(null, JSON.parse(cached));
      
      analytics.track('user_fetched', { userId }, (err) => {
        callback(null, user);
      });
    });
  });
}
```

**After:**

```typescript
// Modern async/await with proper error handling
async function getUserData(userId: string): Promise<User> {
  // Check cache first
  const cached = await cache.get(`user:${userId}`);
  if (cached) {
    return JSON.parse(cached) as User;
  }
  
  // Fetch from database
  const user = await database.query<User>(
    'SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1',
    [userId]
  );
  
  if (!user) {
    throw new NotFoundError(`User ${userId} not found`);
  }
  
  // Cache the result
  await cache.setex(`user:${userId}`, 3600, JSON.stringify(user));
  
  // Track analytics (fire and forget)
  analytics.track('user_fetched', { userId }).catch(logger.error);
  
  return user;
}
```

### Migration Path:

```typescript
// Step 1: Create wrapper that supports both patterns
function promisify<T>(fn: CallbackBasedFn<T>): AsyncFn<T> {
  return function(...args) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      fn(...args, (err, result) => {
        if (err) reject(err);
        else resolve(result);
      });
    });
  };
}

// Step 2: Gradually migrate one function at a time
const getUserDataAsync = promisify(getUserData);

// Step 3: Refactor each function individually
async function getUserDataRefactored(userId: string) {
  // New implementation
}

// Step 4: Remove wrapper once all migrated
```

## Anti Pattern

- [ ] **Big Bang Refactor**: Refactor everything at once
- [ ] **No Tests**: Refactor without test coverage
- [ ] **Scope Creep**: Add features during refactoring
- [ ] **Ignore Breakage**: Continue despite breaking changes
- [ ] **Skip Documentation**: Don't update docs
- [ ] **No Rollback**: No way to revert changes
- [ ] **Parallel Effort**: Refactor while adding features
- [ ] **Perfect Code Syndrome**: Chase perfection, miss deadlines

## Best Practice

- [ ] **Small Increments**: Refactor in small, testable chunks
- [ ] **Test First**: Write tests before refactoring
- [ ] **Continuous Integration**: Run tests on every change
- [ ] **Feature Flags**: Enable changes gradually
- [ ] **Pair Programming**: Two eyes on code
- [ ] **Code Review**: Peer review all changes
- [ ] **Measure Progress**: Track quality metrics
- [ ] **Communicate**: Keep stakeholders informed

